WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.810
- [Narrator] Fertilization
is the epic story

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.790
of a single sperm facing incredible odds

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:12.410
to unite with an egg and
form a new human life,

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.183
it is the story of all of us.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.273
(enigmatic music)

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.260
During sexual intercourse,

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.533
about 300 million sperm enter the vagina.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.780
Soon afterward, millions of
them will either flow out

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.780
of the vagina or die in
its acidic environment.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.630
However, many survive because
of the protective elements

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.713
provided in the fluid surrounding them.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:45.400
Next, the sperm must
pass through the cervix,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.063
and opening into the uterus.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:50.690
Usually, it remains tightly closed,

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.210
but here the cervix is open for a few days

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.733
while the woman ovulates.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:59.120
The sperm swim through the cervical mucus,

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.620
which is thinned to a
more watery consistency

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.843
for easier passage.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.510
Once inside the cervix,

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:09.670
the sperm continues
swimming toward the uterus.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:10.880
Though millions will die

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.570
trying to make it through the mucus,

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.600
some sperm remain behind caught
in the folds of the cervix,

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.290
but they may later continue the journey

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.943
as a backup to the first group.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.090
Inside the uterus, muscular
uterine contractions

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:30.560
assist the sperm on their
journey toward the egg.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.150
However, residents cells from
the women's immune system,

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.620
mistaking the sperm for foreign invaders,

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:38.253
destroy thousands more.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:49.010
Next, half the sperm head
for the empty fallopian tube,

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:51.660
while the other half swim
toward the tube containing

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.450
the unfertilized egg.

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.293
Now, only a few thousand remain.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:58.930
Inside the fallopian tube,

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:02.570
tiny cilia push the egg toward the uterus.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.790
To continue, the sperm must surge

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:07.630
against this motion to reach the egg,

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:11.340
some sperm get trapped
in the cilia and die.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.050
During this part of the journey,

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.030
chemicals in the reproductive
tract cause the membranes

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.010
covering the heads of the sperm to change.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:22.040
As a result, the sperm become hyperactive,

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.093
swimming harder and faster
toward their destination.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.653
At long last, the sperm reach the egg.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:36.933
Only a few dozen of the original
300 million sperm remain.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.070
The egg is covered with a layer of cells

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:41.803
called the corona radiata.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.560
The sperm must push through this layer

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.883
to reach the outer layer of
the egg, the zona pellucida.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.800
When sperm reach the zona
pellucida, they're attached

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.340
to specialized sperm
receptors on the surface

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.303
which triggers their acrosomes
to release digestive enzymes,

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:03.573
enabling the sperm to
burrow into the layer.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:11.200
Inside de zona pellucida is
a narrow, fluid-filled space

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.383
just outside the egg cell membrane.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.533
The first sperm to make
contact will fertilize the egg.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.830
After a perilous journey
and against incredible odds,

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:26.813
a single sperm attaches
to the egg cell membrane.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.170
Within a few minutes,
the outer membranes fuse,

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.283
and the egg pulls the sperm inside.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:38.060
This event causes changes
in the egg membrane

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.573
that prevent other sperm
from attaching to it.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.060
Next, the egg releases chemicals

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:46.570
that push other sperm away from the egg,

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:50.360
and create an impenetrable
fertilization membrane.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:54.350
As the reaction spreads outward,
the zona pellucida hardens

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:57.403
trapping any sperm unlucky
enough to be caught inside.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.610
Outside the egg, sperm are no longer able

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.623
to attach to the zona pellucida.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.450
Meanwhile, inside the egg,

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.493
the tightly-packed male
genetic material spreads out.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.090
A new membrane forms
around the genetic material

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:22.193
creating the male pronucleus.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.763
Inside, the genetic material
reforms into 23 chromosomes.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.570
The female genetic material,

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.290
awakened by the fusion of
the sperm with the egg,

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:37.230
finishes dividing resulting
in the female pronucleus

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:40.730
which also contains 23 chromosomes.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:43.650
As the male and female pronuclei form,

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:47.020
spider-web-like threads
called microtubules

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.583
pull them toward each other.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:53.070
The two sets of chromosomes join together

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:56.260
completing the process of fertilization.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:59.870
At this moment, a unique
genetic code arises,

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:03.080
instantly determining gender, hair color,

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.253
eye color, and hundreds
of other characteristics.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.040
This new single cell, the zygote,

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:12.363
is the beginning of a new human being.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:16.100
And now the cilia and the fallopian tube

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:19.150
gently sweep the zygote toward the uterus

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:22.570
where he or she will implant
in the rich uterine lining.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:25.440
Growing and maturing
for the next nine months

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:26.793
until ready for birth.

00:05:29.749 --> 00:05:32.582
(enigmatic music)

